  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Junco Partner**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Iko Iko / I Feel Like Funkin' It Up**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Take A Chance**: rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **No More Okey Doke**: back after 30 archived shows (735 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Voices Inside (Everything Is Everything)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **I Need More Time**: rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Fire On The Bayou**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **People Say**: back after 29 archived shows (734 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2015-03-20.cmc622xt.sbd.matrix.flac24** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 17 songs; 150 min [1]\n- **soulive2015-03-20.cmc622xt.sbd.matrix.flac16**: matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 17 songs; 150 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The show was Night 7 of the Bowlive VI run at Brooklyn Bowl [1]\n- The show was Night 7 of Bowlive VI at Brooklyn Bowl [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2015-03-20.cmc622xt.sbd.matrix.flac24**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: On Stage Audience/SBD Matrix [1]. Also: Recorded with on-stage Schoeps cmc622xt mics, split at 15 feet, matrixed with a soundboard feed from a Digidesign/Avid Profile console; Both sources captured on a Sound Devices 744T at 24-bit/96k, time-aligned in SoundForge Pro 11 and mixed in Vegas Pro 13 [1]\n- **soulive2015-03-20.cmc622xt.sbd.matrix.flac16**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: On Stage Audience/SBD Matrix [2]. Also: Matrix of on-stage Schoeps cmc622xt mics (split 15') and a Digidesign/Avid Profile soundboard feed, recorded on a Sound Devices 744T; This 16-bit version was downsampled from 96k to 44.1k with iZotope SRC and dithered with MBIT+, then converted to FLAC [2]",
